      "mergeID": "633b0f3854142e76e3e64232",
      "mergedPostDetails": "My current launch options (somewhat leftovers):\n--legacy-fbt-calibrate --fps=144 --affinity=FFF000\nUsing new menu option 'Legacy Calibration' for FBT calibration prevents any avatar (only tested with default locomotion layer on AV3 avatars) from being able to move/locomote. \nTested in multiple worlds.\nObserved in 6pt tracking after switching avatar without re-calibration, also happens in desktop upon loading into any world once the setting is enabled in VR, therefore preventing any desktop-mode locomotion. Switching it off (\"new\" calibration) does not do this. Also re-enables locomotion upon recalibration in an avatar, but bug reoccurs after switching avatar.\nAny other relevant details I might be missing may be requested.\n\nEDIT: Also of note, as you may be able to see above, I had legacy calibration enabled before this update, where it worked as intended last build.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1244] FBT Legacy Calibration menu option prevents avatar locomotion",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
